[Slide 1 – What is VR?]
"Thank you. Now I will talk about Virtual Reality, or VR.
Virtual Reality is a technology that puts you inside a digital world. You wear a special headset and suddenly, you are no longer in the room. You are in a game, a mountain, a space station — anywhere.
You can look left, right, up, down — and the world moves with you. It feels very real."

[Slide 2 – How it Works]
"So how does VR work?
The headset has two small screens — one for each eye. This creates a feeling of depth, like real life. It also has sensors that track your head movement. Some VR systems also have controllers so you can use your hands in the virtual world."

Slide 3 – VR in Gaming]
"In gaming, VR is changing everything.
Instead of watching a character on a screen, you ARE the character. You fight, explore, and solve puzzles with your whole body. Games like Beat Saber and Resident Evil Village VR are very popular examples.
Players say VR feels more exciting and more emotional than normal games."

[Slide 4 – Beyond Gaming]
"VR is not only for games.
It is also used in education — students can visit ancient Rome or go inside the human body. It is used in medicine — doctors practice surgery in VR before touching a real patient. It is also used in sports training and therapy.
This shows that VR is a very powerful technology."

[Transition to next speaker]
"So, Virtual Reality is already changing how we play and learn — and it will only get better. Now, my teammate Andrew will talk about Cloud Gaming."
